{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Patchset 2 pushed on Gerrit change 1771 (same Change-Id I7996314ac61587198e3e3b6aedf75dd69699fd23), rebased onto origin/main ce54970555. Fixes the Verified -1: the raw-git-writes policy gate (scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py, merged after my original base) flagged doctor's update-ref and checkout calls — both ARE the sanctioned repair door, so they now carry inline '# raw-git-ok: <reason>' markers on the enclosing defs (backup-ref audit envelope mirroring tracker-maintenance; checkout-restore under the scoped write_lock). Gate passes locally with zero findings. Also folded in 3 of the 5 advisory LLM-Review findings: (1) classifier now uses git status --porcelain -z so C-quoted paths (spaces/quotes/non-ASCII) arrive verbatim, with rename/copy source records skipped; (2) fsck dirty lines shlex-quote paths and the JSON parser uses the declared count to locate the path-list/blurb boundary — text-to-JSON round-trip now lossless (new test with space-containing paths, RED against the old join); (3) the two untested safety contracts got tests: no-backup-ref refuses every mutation + skips reconverge + exits 1; failed checkout/quarantine mark unrepairable with reason + exit 1. Deferred with reply: rename-state (R/AD/MD) deletion classification — outside the observed wedge class, needs its own analysis. Test file now 14 tests, all green; make lint (ratchet new=0 increased=0), make typecheck (539 files), raw-git gate, and fsck/doctor suites (179+26) all clean. Awaiting fresh votes on patchset 2."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786721541125452001,"uuid":"979e36a2-0909-4a9a-a49d-21593c68c092"}